INT. PAWNSHOP - NIGHT

Cluttered shelves. Guitars hang from the ceiling. A glass counter. A cage separates the till.

DETECTIVE MARLOWE-DIAZ (40s, rumpled raincoat) leans on the counter. Behind it, the owner, SOLOMON ABRAMS (60s, green eyeshade), polishes a watch. By the guitars stands TIPPER JOHNSON (20s, nervous, hands in his pockets). In the corner, a woman in a red scarf, CLEOPATRA "CLEO" DUBOIS (30s, calm), examines a ring.

DET. MARLOWE-DIAZ
Evening, Solomon.

SOLOMON
Detective.

DET. MARLOWE-DIAZ
Heard you got a delivery.

SOLOMON
I get many.

The door chimes. A tall man in a trench coat enters, dripping: VICTOR STANHOPE (50s, silver hair, soft hat). He tips the hat to nobody.

VICTOR
Gentlemen. Lady.

MARLOWE-DIAZ
Mr. Stanhope. Out late.

VICTOR
Always.

TIPPER
(whispering)
That's him.

Cleo sets down the ring. Solomon sets down the watch. Nobody moves.

MARLOWE-DIAZ
(quietly)
Tipper. Who?

TIPPER
Nobody.

CLEO
(to Victor)
You're early.

VICTOR
So are you.

Marlowe-Diaz looks from one to the other, then at the safe behind the counter. The lock gleams.

FADE OUT.
